WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.260
Jurassic World is back in a huge way with
new dinosaurs, Baby Blue and Ian Malcolm himself

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.380
in the first full trailer for Fallen Kingdom.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.950
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm breaking down the Jurassic World

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.750
2 trailer for easter eggs, things you missed
and explaining the new dinosaurs you can look

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.570
forward to in the movie!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.620
And if you're new to my channel, I do movie
breakdowns, easter eggs, deleted scenes and

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.570
movie-making secrets, as well as regular giveaways
for all my subscribers.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.460
For my current giveaway, just make sure you're
subscribed and leave me a comment on this

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.990
video with your thoughts about Fallen Kingdom.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.800
I'll have more details on that plus the winner
of my last giveaway later in the video.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.620
The trailer begins with Owen and Claire who
are setting up a task force to save the dinosaurs

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.740
left on the island from a dormant volcano
that's about to explode.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.220
Claire is putting together a new organization
called the Dinosaur Protection Group and,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.579
in the trailer, we get a glimpse of some of
the group's other key members.

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:56.730
We've got a new young scientist played by
Justice Smith, and it's rumoured he's playing

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:02.750
a character inspired by Arby Benton from author
Michael Crichton's second Jurassic Park novel.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:07.170
In another shot, we get a glimpse of Ted Levine's
character who seems to be dressed in combat

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.760
gear and behind him is Daniella Pineda's character.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:15.350
We don't yet have names for their characters,
but in a picture of Pineda released in a behind-the-scenes

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.900
trailer reel, you can see she's got a tattoo
which partially reads "Semper Fi", which is

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:24.640
the US Marine Corps motto, meaning she's likely
either from the US military or she's a former

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.710
marine.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.560
We then get to the island where it's clear
that, since the events of Jurassic World,

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.560
the theme park is more or less in ruins and
dinosaurs are roaming freely.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.760
By the way, the official synopsis states that
the sequel is actually set 4 years after the

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.980
first Jurassic World movie.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:44.100
And back from Jurassic World is our favourite
raptor Blue who, at the end of that movie,

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.170
disappeared into the jungle after helping
Rexy defeat the Indominus.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.030
Also in this next shot of Blue reuniting with
Owen, there's an abandoned old explorer from

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:54.390
the original Jurassic Park movie in the background.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:59.049
Earlier in the trailer, there was also an
adorable short scene of Owen with Baby Blue.

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:02.369
We don't yet know where this comes in the
film, however, I think this might be some

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:07.620
old video of Owen raising baby Blue and imprinting
on her, which he talked about doing in Jurassic

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.620
World.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:12.020
And I think this footage might get played
if Owen gives testimony at this committee

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.120
meeting where we see none other than Ian Malcolm
himself!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.700
Now, we did get some Ian Malcolm easter eggs
in Jurassic World, but this is the moment

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.350
a lot of fans of the franchise have been waiting
for and, of course, Jeff Goldblum even gets

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.180
to deliver his classic line "life finds a
way".

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.670
He's in what looks like either a US government
senate hearing or a courtroom, and I imagine

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.520
he's been called upon as an expert witness,
presumably to comment on the events of Jurassic

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.590
World or perhaps to advise what to do about
the dinosaurs still at large on Isla Nublar.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.640
That seems rather ironic because, in the original
movies, when Malcolm tried to tell the public

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.150
about what had happened at Jurassic Park,
he was discredited by John Hammond's nephew,

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.920
made a laughing stock, and his career was
ruined.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.890
We don't yet know from the limited lines we
hear in the trailer whether Malcolm is for

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.250
or against saving the dinos on the island.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:01.870
Although this is the only scene we've seen
of him so far, I'm hoping we see him pop up

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:06.260
at least once again, though he might just
have a small role appearing near the start

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.290
and the end of the movie, like John Hammond
did in The Lost World.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:13.370
OK, let's get back to the island where we're
going to see some of the new dinosaurs and

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.310
some more call-backs to the original Jurassic
Park.

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:21.090
When we see Claire and her crew hiding behind
some tree trunks from a herd of charging dinos,

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.350
it's an homage to that memorable scene in
the first Jurassic Park movie of Dr Grant

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.520
and the children hiding behind a tree trunk
to avoid a dinosaur stampede.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.500
And just at this moment we get our first look
at the Carnotaurus, a new dinosaur for the

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.500
sequel.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.220
The Carnotaurus, which means "meat-eating
bull", has two horns above its eyes, and,

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:44.460
fun fact, genetic material from the Carnotaurus
was used for the creation of the hybrid Indominus

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.410
Rex in the first Jurassic World.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:51.060
Now, this is one pretty mean-looking dino
but just as it seems to be about to take out

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.871
Owen and the others, Rexy swoops in and saves
the day.

00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:57.651
And if you're thinking that there seems to
be something familiar about this scene, it's

00:03:57.651 --> 00:04:02.170
because it's clearly a tribute to the final
scene in Jurassic Park where the T-Rex roars

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:05.970
after saving the adults and kids from the
velociraptors.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.450
Another new dinosaur which was only hinted
at in Jurassic World, but which we're getting

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.220
properly in Fallen Kingdom, is the Baryonyx.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.510
The name refers to the "heavy, large claw"
on the dino's first finger, and it was going

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:21.230
to be the original primary antagonist in the
third Jurassic Park movie, until it was replaced

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.540
by the Spinosaurus.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.800
And it looks like the Baryonyx will make a
spectacular appearance during an underground

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.210
scene in what is probably a control room for
an old power plant on the island.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.380
You can see fire and lava flowing, so it looks
like this scene takes place around the time

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.740
the volcano begins to erupt.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.810
We know now that Rexy is back for the sequel
and, in another shot, we can see she's been

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.040
sedated and loaded into a truck.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.380
And although we see what looks like a lot
of dinosaurs probably perishing from the volcano

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.030
eruption, there are a few shots earlier in
the trailer that show what looks like a boat,

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.210
loaded with dinosaurs, leaving the island.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:58.330
Now, if you're concerned you've seen most
of the movie's plot, rest assured that these

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.290
scenes are actually only from the first half
of the movie and are, in a sense, the set-up

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.080
for the main plot of the film.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.130
The official synopsis has actually stated
that Claire and Owen uncover "a conspiracy

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:13.580
that could return our entire planet to a perilous
order not seen since prehistoric times."

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.960
Which means, I think, that there's a plot
going on to bring these dinosaurs off the

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.010
island and to the mainland.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:23.010
InGen will likely be involved in this together
with Henry Wu who we didn't get to see in

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.100
this trailer.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.550
Dr Wu was last seen in Jurassic World on an
InGen helicopter making off with a bunch of

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:33.460
dinosaur DNA from the park, however, in the
Fallen Kingdom behind-the-scenes reel, we

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:38.200
did get a brief glimpse of Wu who's definitely
cooking up a new hybrid, the Indo-raptor,

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.700
which I expect we'll see later in the film.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.290
By the way, all the footage released so far
suggests we're getting a much bigger push

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:46.860
for animatronic dinosaurs in Fallen Kingdom.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.320
Practical effects were a big part of the original
Jurassic Park movie, whereas the first Jurassic

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:55.890
World movie only used animatronics in a single
scene with a dying Apatosaurus.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:06:00.010
The animatronics development on the sequel
has been spearheaded by Neal Scanlan, whose

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.410
creature designs you'll have seen in the new
Star Wars movies.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.940
Animatronics will be limited mostly to close-up
shots, with CGI enhancing some elements, but

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.430
from what's been teased so far it looks good.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.640
Now, what did you think of the first full
trailer for Fallen Kingdom?

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:18.260
Were you a fan of the first movie and has
the new trailer got you hyped for the sequel?

